# Round six, item language (I3): the interior of a node

Under a node assignment (`NodeRH`), given implementations of the steps of the network (constant
costs `cf a`, widths `dwf a`) and of the leftover call (cost `cR`, width `DWR`), the interior of
`nodeC`

  `padCU 23 21 (steps) ; (leftover frame; call jL) ; scaleQ 23 23 25 26`

implements `tens Cm` on the `E` bits (scale `∑ eStH + (Gs (E mod m) + δ)`), with cost
`≤ ∑ cf + cR + 10^17 · W' n' Y` on the whole window (**`sImplQ_nodeIn`**).
